# Kafka Java style

Follow the checks already enforced in this repo. Do not weaken them to land a change.

## License header

Every new or edited Java file starts with the header in `checkstyle/java.header`. Checkstyle's `Header` module compares that file byte for byte. There is no blank line between the header and `package`.

## Layout and Checkstyle

Rules live in `checkstyle/checkstyle.xml`. Import control is per module (`checkstyle/import-control*.xml`). The global file disallows `kafka.*` from `org.apache.kafka` and says to think hard before changing layering.

- 4-space indent, no tabs (`FileTabCharacter`). K&R braces (`LeftCurly`, `RightCurly`).
- One statement per line. No star imports (`AvoidStarImport`).
- No `System.exit`. Use `Exit.exit` (Checkstyle id `dontUseSystemExit`).
- No `toLowerCase()` / `toUpperCase()` without a `Locale` argument.
- Constants are `UPPER_SNAKE`. The logger field is the Checkstyle exception: name it `log`.
- Complexity caps: method length 170, parameters 13, cyclomatic complexity 16, NPath 500, boolean expression complexity 5, JavaNCSS method size 100.
- `FinalLocalVariable` (including parameters and enhanced-for variables) is enforced under `org.apache.kafka.streams`. Prefer `final` locals elsewhere too.
- Do not add a `checkstyle/suppressions.xml` entry to silence a new violation.

## Imports

Checkstyle does not order imports. Spotless does (`build.gradle`):

`kafka`, `org.apache.kafka`, `com`, `net`, `org`, `java`, `javax`, then everything else, then static imports.

Blank line between groups. Run `./gradlew spotlessApply` on the modules you touched, then `checkstyleMain` / `checkstyleTest`.

## Logging

SLF4J only. Log4j and `System.out` are not the project logger.

```java
private static final Logger log = LoggerFactory.getLogger(TheClass.class);
```

Parameterized messages, with the throwable last:

```java
log.warn("Failed to load metadata for topic {}", topic, exception);
```

Do not concatenate arguments into the message string. Do not log secrets, credentials, or full record payloads.

## Language level

`javac --release` is 11 for `:clients`, `:generator`, `:streams`, `:streams:test-utils`, `:streams:examples`, `:streams:streams-scala`, and `:test-common:test-common-util`. It is 17 everywhere else. Do not use APIs newer than that module's release level, and do not use preview features.

## Generated sources

Do not hand-edit `**/generated/**` or `**/generated-test/**`. Change the message specs under `clients/src/main/resources/common/message/` and regenerate with `./gradlew processMessages processTestMessages`.
